WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.402
With the foreperson that

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.603
the jury has selected.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.473
Please stand and state your number

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.041
over 19.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.410
Thank you.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.113
Has the jury reached a verdict?

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.948
Will you please hand it to the bailiff?

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.484
And the bailiff will bring it to me.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.385
Thank you.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:43.343
You may be seated.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:48.648
Thank you.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.418
Will now have the clerk read the verdict.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.219
You can just read the question.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:53.953
Answer?

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.354
Yes.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.322
Okay.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.494
Was Gwyneth Paltrow at fault?

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.430
No.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.164
Was Gwyneth

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.198
Paltrow's fault

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:09.736
a cause of Terry Sanderson's harm?

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:10.570
Oh,

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.841
there's just no response there.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.110
Was Terry Sanderson at fault?

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.647
Yes, it was Terry Sanderson's fault.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.483
Cause Gwyneth Paltrow

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.084
did.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.019
Did Terry Sanderson's fault cause

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.454
Gwyneth Paltrow's harm?

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.823
Yes.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.859
Comparative fault.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.494
What percent of the fault

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.696
do you assign to Terry Sanderson?

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:40.066
100%

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.602
damages.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.470
What amount?

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.737
Fairly commensurate

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.773
can compensate Gwyneth Paltrow

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.708
for economic damages?

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.743
$1 nice.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.547
Signed March 30th, 2023.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.351
Thank you.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:01:59.419
So to

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.687
to juror number 19,

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.555
the foreperson, is this your verdict?

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.858
Yes, sir. Thank you.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:05.992
And the attorneys have asked

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.128
that I pull the jury and I

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.662
so I need to ask each one of you

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.698
if this is your verdict.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.766
This is not an unusual thing to happen.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.435
It happens quite often.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.437
So number 16, is this your verdict?

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.638
Yes, your honor.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.572
Thank you.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:21.508
Number 11, is this your verdict?

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.842
Yes, Your Honor.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.777
Number eight, is this your verdict?

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.045
Yes, your honor.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.914
Number two, is this your verdict?

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:28.948
Yes, sure.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.818
I've already covered number 19.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.753
Number 28. Is this your verdict?

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.587
Yes, Your Honor.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.056
Number 29. Is this your verdict?

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:37.891
Yes, Your Honor.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.993
And number 32, is this your verdict?

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.761
Yes, Your Honor. Thank you.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.330
So to the attorneys, is there

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.165
anything further

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.334
before I discharged the jury

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.036
for the plaintiff? No.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.638
Thank you, Your Honor. Okay.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:52.539
Thank you.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.141
Let me just read you

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.377
the last jury instruction.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.811
Ladies and gentlemen of the jury,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.147
this trial is finished.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.249
Thank you for your service.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.486
The American system of justice relies

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.788
on your time and your sound judgment.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:13.026
And you have been generous with both.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.260
You serve justice

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.496
by your fair and impartial decision.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.765
I hope you found the experience

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:19.966
rewarding.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.100
You may now

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.302
talk about this case

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.337
with anyone you like.

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.673
You may be contacted by the press

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.541
or by the lawyers.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.110
You do not have to talk to them

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.513
or with anyone else, but you may.

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:37.250
The choice is entirely yours.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.851
I turn now to the lawyers

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.322
and to the press

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.490
and ask them to honor your wishes.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.491
If you say that

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:48.528
you do not want to talk about the case,

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:51.030
if you do decide to talk about the case,

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.233
please respect the privacy

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.535
of your fellow jurors.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:56.002
The Court

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:56.936
The confidences

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.471
that they may have shared with you

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.006
while deliberating

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.809
are not yours to share with others.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.144
Again, thank you for your service.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:08.915
You may now retire.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:09.849
And if everybody else would

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:10.950
please remain here.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.785
We've got some things to do.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.754
All right. The jury.

